          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## September 2025 close review\n\n- **Work order:** `WO-2025-09-004` — `MO-25-09-1070`\n- **Cost event:** `CE-250904-0004` (`INPUT`)\n- **Source transaction:** `TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070`\n- **Amount:** **28,476,342 cents** (**$284,763.42**)\n- **Event-created time:** `2025-09-30T19:15:00`\n- **September period Pending Close time:** `2025-09-30T18:00:00`\n- **Lateness:** **75 minutes** (1 hour 15 minutes after Pending Close)\n- **Recorded accounting status:** `POSTED`\n\n### Conclusion\n\nYes. The component-input event was created after the September cost period entered Pending Close. Oracle’s documented treatment states that transactions created after the Pending Close date aren’t processed or staged, except for specified categories such as revenue, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments. This event was an `INPUT`, not an exception category.\n\nTherefore, the recorded `POSTED` status is **not consistent** with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment.\n\nThe review was read-only; no database records were changed. Source evidence: task records `r_3b47185690520ace21c00de8` and `r_c5101a84b7863959f8da52a0`; policy excerpt from *oracle_supply_chain_cost_management_26b.pdf*, PDF page 233.",
